From nobody Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dawid Wesierski <dawid.wesierski@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:18:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net/ixgbe: keep E610 PHY powered at port stop

ixgbe_dev_stop() puts the copper PHY in low power. On E610 the next
ixgbe_dev_start() takes it out with an ACI Set PHY Config (0x0601), and
the firmware restarts the autoneg. For 50 to 100 ms Get Link Status
still reports the old link as up, then the link is down for about
4.7 s. An application that starts to transmit at the link up of the
start sees no packet leave for that time.

Measured on an E610 10GBASE-T port, link up before the start: the
start sent one 0x0601, the link read up for 5 ms, down 81 ms after the
start and up again after 4.68 s, and the first packets waited 4.7 s.
With the PHY powered on 8 s before the start, the start sent no 0x0601,
the link stayed up, and 314 of 314 packets left from 0.147 s.

The Linux ixgbe driver powers the PHY off in ixgbe_down() only for an
interface that goes down with no wake on LAN, so a reset does not
restart the autoneg. Keep the E610 PHY powered at the port stop, and so
at the close. rte_eth_dev_set_link_down() still powers it off.

Signed-off-by: Dawid Wesierski <dawid.wesierski@intel.com>
---
 drivers/net/intel/ixgbe/ixgbe_ethdev.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/intel/ixgbe/ixgbe_ethdev.c b/drivers/net/intel/ixgbe/ixgbe_ethdev.c
index c5010f623c..cbcfa2d871 100644
--- a/drivers/net/intel/ixgbe/ixgbe_ethdev.c
+++ b/drivers/net/intel/ixgbe/ixgbe_ethdev.c
@@ -2965,8 +2965,13 @@ ixgbe_dev_stop(struct rte_eth_dev *dev)
 		vfinfo[vf].clear_to_send = false;
 
 	if (hw->mac.ops.get_media_type(hw) == ixgbe_media_type_copper) {
-		/* Turn off the copper */
-		ixgbe_set_phy_power(hw, false);
+		/*
+		 * Turn off the copper, but not on E610: the power on at the
+		 * next start restarts its autoneg. Keep it on, as Linux
+		 * ixgbe_down() does when WoL is on.
+		 */
+		if (hw->mac.type != ixgbe_mac_E610)
+			ixgbe_set_phy_power(hw, false);
 	} else {
 		/* Turn off the laser */
 		ixgbe_disable_tx_laser(hw);
